  </diagram>
  <diagram id="build" name="2. Build: Makefile → CMake → firmware">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1396" dy="808" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="850" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="build-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:22px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;From source code to a flashed board&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Example: mini_rover_stm32g431cbu6/. PDB_24 works the same way. Hover for details.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="900" x="40" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="← back to overview" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Click (or Ctrl+click while editing) to go back to the overview page.&lt;/div&gt;" link="data:page/id,overview" id="build-back">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="30" width="120" x="960" y="30" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;You&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;make build&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;make flash&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;You run this in the board&#39;s folder. `make help` lists the targets.&lt;/div&gt;" id="s1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="110" width="180" x="40" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Makefile&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Shortcut list. Runs the long cmake commands for you.&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Makefile targets (mini_rover):&lt;br&gt;• configure: cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=cmake/gcc-arm-none-eabi.cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug&lt;br&gt;• build: configure, then cmake --build build&lt;br&gt;• flash: build, then st-flash ... write build/mini_rover.bin 0x08000000&lt;br&gt;• flash-ocd: same but with OpenOCD&lt;br&gt;• clean / rebuild&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Make itself is a decades-old tool: a target name, what it depends on, and the shell commands to run.&lt;/div&gt;" id="s2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="110" width="180" x="255" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bs1" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="s2" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;CMake&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Reads CMakeLists.txt.&lt;br&gt;Decides &lt;i&gt;what&lt;/i&gt; to compile and &lt;i&gt;how&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Writes build/build.ninja&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;(configure: no compiling yet)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;CMake is a build-system generator: it doesn&#39;t compile anything itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It reads:&lt;br&gt;• CMakeLists.txt (your sources + include folders, see below)&lt;br&gt;• cmake/stm32cubemx/CMakeLists.txt (CubeMX&#39;s file list + HAL_Drivers)&lt;br&gt;• cmake/gcc-arm-none-eabi.cmake (the toolchain file: use the ARM cross-compiler and chip flags)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;...and writes instructions for Ninja into build/build.ninja.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is the CONFIGURE step. It doesn&#39;t compile anything; it only plans the build. (build/ is just the output folder&#39;s name.)&lt;/div&gt;" id="s3">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="110" width="180" x="470" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bs2" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="s3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Ninja + arm-none-eabi-gcc&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;(build: the actual compiling)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Compiles every .c/.cpp → .o, links them into &lt;i&gt;mini_rover.elf&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Ninja runs the compiler commands, only re-compiling files that changed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;arm-none-eabi-gcc is a CROSS-compiler: it runs on your PC but produces machine code for the STM32&#39;s ARM Cortex-M4 core.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;.o = one compiled file. Linking glues all .o files into one program (.elf), using the linker script (.ld) to place code in flash and variables in RAM.&lt;/div&gt;" id="s4">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="110" width="180" x="685" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bs3" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="s4" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;.elf → .bin → board&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;objcopy strips it to raw bytes; st-flash writes them over the ST-Link&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;.elf: the program plus debug info (what a debugger uses).&lt;br&gt;.bin: just the raw bytes that go into flash, made by objcopy (POST_BUILD step at the bottom of CMakeLists.txt).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;`make flash` uses st-flash to write the .bin to address 0x08000000 (start of STM32 flash) over an ST-Link programmer.&lt;/div&gt;" id="s5">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="110" width="180" x="900" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bs4" edge="1" parent="1" source="s4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="s5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cml" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Inside a board&#39;s CMakeLists.txt&lt;/b&gt;: the parts you edit most&lt;div&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="330" width="640" x="40" y="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cml1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;" value="&lt;b&gt;target_sources(...)&lt;/b&gt;: which .c/.cpp files get compiled" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="600" x="60" y="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlA" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Core/Src/app/app_main.cpp&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;this board&#39;s app&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="190" x="60" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlB" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;${COMMON_LIBS_PATH}/&lt;br&gt;clock/timer.cpp&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;generic libs&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="190" x="265" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlC" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;${PLATFORM_PATH}/Modules/&lt;br&gt;clock/clock_stm32g4xx.cpp&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;STM32 implementations&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="190" x="470" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cml2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;" value="&lt;b&gt;target_include_directories(...)&lt;/b&gt;: folders searched when code says &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;#include &quot;timer.hpp&quot;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="600" x="60" y="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlD" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Core/Inc/...&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="48" width="190" x="60" y="430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlE" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;${COMMON_LIBS_PATH}/&lt;br&gt;clock&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="48" width="190" x="265" y="430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cmlF" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;${PLATFORM_PATH}/&lt;br&gt;Modules/clock&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="48" width="190" x="470" y="430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cml3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adding a library to a board&lt;/b&gt; = add its .cpp to target_sources &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; its folder to target_include_directories. A .cpp that isn&#39;t listed is never compiled (you&#39;ll get an &#39;undefined reference&#39; link error). A folder that isn&#39;t listed gives &#39;No such file or directory&#39; on #include.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Paths at the top: &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;COMMON_LIBS_PATH&lt;/font&gt; = ../common_libraries, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;PLATFORM_PATH&lt;/font&gt; = ../platform/stm32g4xx&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;This can be simplified with a common cmakelists that just includes all common libraries by default...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="600" x="60" y="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;common_libraries/ has its own Makefile + CMakeLists&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;...but they build for &lt;b&gt;your PC&lt;/b&gt;, not a board:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;cd common_libraries&lt;br&gt;make test&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;→ compiles the libraries + every test/test_*.cpp with g++&lt;br&gt;→ links Catch2 (submodules/Catch2)&lt;br&gt;→ runs them with ctest&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;GitHub Actions runs this on every push. Board projects &lt;b&gt;don&#39;t&lt;/b&gt; use this CMakeLists. They list the common .cpp files themselves.&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Why two kinds of build?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Firmware must be cross-compiled for the STM32 and can only run on the board.&lt;br&gt;Hardware-agnostic code can ALSO be compiled for your PC, where it is fast and easy to test automatically. That&#39;s the main payoff of keeping common_libraries free of HAL calls.&lt;/div&gt;" id="clb">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="330" width="340" x="710" y="260" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="gloss" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Jargon&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Toolchain / cross-compiler&lt;/b&gt;: compiler that runs on your PC but outputs code for another CPU (arm-none-eabi-gcc).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Configure&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;i&gt;cmake -B build&lt;/i&gt;): CMake reads the CMakeLists and writes a to-do list for Ninja (build/build.ninja). &lt;u&gt;Nothing is compiled yet.&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Build&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;i&gt;cmake --build build&lt;/i&gt;): runs Ninja, which actually calls the compiler. &lt;i&gt;make build&lt;/i&gt; does both.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ninja&lt;/b&gt;: fast tool that runs the compile commands.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CMakePresets.json&lt;/b&gt;: saved configure settings, used by the VS Code CMake extension instead of the Makefile.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CubeMX&lt;/b&gt;: ST&#39;s tool that generates chip setup code from the .ioc file. Re-generating can overwrite files outside USER CODE blocks.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="1010" x="40" y="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="iface" name="3. Interfaces vs implementations">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1712" dy="1060" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="850" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="iface-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:22px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Interfaces vs implementations: the clock example&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Interface = WHAT (a promise). Implementation = HOW (on one specific chip). Generic code only ever talks to the interface.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="900" x="40" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="← back to overview" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Click (or Ctrl+click while editing) to go back to the overview page.&lt;/div&gt;" link="data:page/id,overview" id="iface-back">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="30" width="120" x="960" y="30" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;«interface»&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ClockInterface&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;virtual ClockStatus init() = 0;&lt;br&gt;virtual uint32_t get_ms() = 0;&lt;br&gt;virtual void blocking_delay(uint32_t ms) = 0;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot; color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;common_libraries/clock/clock_interface.hpp&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;An interface (in C++: an abstract class).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;`virtual ... = 0` means PURE VIRTUAL: the function is declared but has no body here. You can&#39;t create a ClockInterface object directly, only an object of a class that fills these in.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;No #include of any STM32/HAL header, so this file compiles anywhere.&lt;/div&gt;" id="ci">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="150" width="330" x="345" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Timer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Timer(ClockInterface&amp;amp; clock, ...);&lt;br&gt;set(ms) / expired() / restart()&lt;/font&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Only knows &quot;some clock&quot;. Never sees STM32 code.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot; color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;common_libraries/clock/timer.hpp&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Generic library code.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Timer stores a reference to a ClockInterface and calls clock.get_ms(). It doesn&#39;t know or care whether that&#39;s an STM32 SysTick, an ESP32 timer, or a fake clock in a unit test.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Because of that, the same timer.cpp is compiled into every board.&lt;/div&gt;" id="timer">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="150" width="290" x="760" y="110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;ClockSTM32G4XX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;: public ClockInterface&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;uint32_t get_ms() override {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;return HAL_GetTick();&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot; color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;platform/stm32g4xx/Modules/clock/clock_stm32g4xx.cpp&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;An implementation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;`: public ClockInterface` = inherits from the interface (&quot;I am a ClockInterface&quot;).&lt;br&gt;`override` = &quot;this is my body for one of the interface&#39;s functions&quot;; the compiler errors if the name/signature doesn&#39;t match.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is the ONLY place that calls ST&#39;s HAL_GetTick() / HAL_Delay(). It includes stm32g4xx_hal.h, which is why it lives in platform/, not common_libraries/.&lt;/div&gt;" id="cs">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="150" width="330" x="345" y="360" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;ClockESP32&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;FakeClock&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;: public ClockInterface&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Don&#39;t exist yet.&lt;/i&gt; Shows the payoff: add one of these and Timer works on a new chip, or in a PC unit test, with zero changes.&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;Hypothetical.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• platform/esp32/Modules/clock/clock_esp32.cpp would make Timer usable on ESP32 boards.&lt;br&gt;• A FakeClock in a test file (get_ms() returns a number the test controls) would let Catch2 test Timer on your PC without any hardware or waiting.&lt;/div&gt;" id="fake">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;spacingTop=4;dashed=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="150" width="270" x="40" y="360" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;app_main.cpp&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;(PDB_24 board project)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;ClockSTM32G4XX clock;&lt;br&gt;Timer minute_timer(clock, true);&lt;/font&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;The board picks the real implementation and hands it to the generic code. &lt;b&gt;Ideally, this only takes in interfaces, and doesn&#39;t rely on platform, so we can unit test it.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:520px;padding:4px&quot;&gt;PDB_24/Core/Src/app/app_main.cpp lines 28-29.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is DEPENDENCY INJECTION: instead of Timer creating its own clock (and so being tied to STM32), the board creates the clock and passes (&#39;injects&#39;) it into Timer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The board project is the one place where &#39;which hardware?&#39; gets decided.&lt;/div&gt;" id="app">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="150" width="290" x="760" y="360" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="ie1" edge="1" parent="1" source="cs" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=block;endFill=0;endSize=12;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="ci" value="implements">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ie2" edge="1" parent="1" source="fake" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=block;endFill=0;endSize=12;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="ci" value="implements">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="-0.2464" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="175" y="185" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ie3" edge="1" parent="1" source="timer" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="ci" value="uses">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ie4" edge="1" parent="1" source="app" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="cs" value="creates">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ie5" edge="1" parent="1" source="app" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" target="timer" value="creates, passes&lt;br&gt;clock in">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ip-gloss" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;spacing=8;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Jargon&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Interface / abstract class&lt;/b&gt;: a class that only declares functions (all &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;= 0&lt;/font&gt;).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pure virtual&lt;/b&gt;: a function with no body that subclasses must provide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;I&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;mplementation / concrete class&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;: a subclass that provides every body.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;override&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;: marks a function as filling in a virtual one (cpp keyword).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;Hardware-agnostic&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;: doesn&#39;t depend on any specific chip.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;Dependency injection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;: passing in the thing you depend on rather than creating it yourself.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The pattern as a whole is often called a &lt;i&gt;hardware abstraction layer&lt;/i&gt;; ST&#39;s HAL is the same idea one level lower.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="1010" x="40" y="550" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
